---
// "Design by elimination" from chapter 1: with a fixed scale (12 / 16 / 24 / 32 px) you guess one
// value and compare its two neighbours instead of agonising over every pixel.
// Squares are drawn at 2x so the size difference is visible. Plain inline SVG, site tokens.

const W = 900;
const H = 290;
const sizes = [12, 16, 24, 32];
const k = 2;
const cx = [140, 330, 520, 710];
const baseline = 100;
const picked = 16;
---
<figure class="sel">
  <div class="sel-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="A scale of four icon sizes: 12, 16, 24 and 32 pixels. Guess 16, then compare it with 12 and 24, the neighbours on each side. If both look clearly wrong, 16 is the answer.">
      {sizes.map((s, i) => {
        const side = s * k;
        return (
          <g class:list={['sel-item', { 'is-pick': s === picked }]}>
            <rect x={cx[i] - side / 2} y={baseline - side} width={side} height={side} rx={side / 6} />
            <text x={cx[i]} y={baseline + 26} text-anchor="middle">{s} px</text>
          </g>
        );
      })}

      <path class="sel-bracket" d={`M ${cx[0] - 36} 150 L ${cx[0] - 36} 160 L ${cx[2] + 36} 160 L ${cx[2] + 36} 150`} />
      <text x={(cx[0] + cx[2]) / 2} y="184" text-anchor="middle" class="sel-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Guess 16, then look at the neighbour on each side</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Đoán 16, rồi so với hai bên cạnh nó</tspan>
      </text>

      <text x="60" y="226" class="sel-line">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Both neighbours look clearly worse: 16 is your answer, stop here.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Cả hai bên đều rõ ràng tệ hơn: chọn 16, dừng ở đây.</tspan>
      </text>
      <text x="60" y="252" class="sel-line">
        <tspan data-lang-en>24 looks best: repeat with 16, 24 and 32, with 24 in the middle.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>24 trông đẹp nhất: lặp lại với 16, 24, 32, lấy 24 làm điểm giữa.</tspan>
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Four options that all look different are easy to rank. Squares are drawn at twice their pixel size.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Bốn lựa chọn nhìn khác hẳn nhau thì rất dễ xếp hạng. Các ô vuông được vẽ gấp đôi kích thước pixel thật.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .sel {
    margin: 2em 0;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .sel-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .sel svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 640px;
    height: auto;
  }
  .sel text {
    font-size: 14px;
    fill: var(--text-body);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .sel-item rect {
    fill: var(--bg-alt);
    stroke: var(--text-muted);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .sel-item.is-pick rect {
    fill: var(--red-tint-bg);
    stroke: var(--red);
  }
  .sel-item.is-pick text {
    fill: var(--red);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .sel-bracket {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--text-muted);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .sel text.sel-h {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: var(--text);
  }
  .sel text.sel-line {
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .sel figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.6em;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
